      "final": "Verified with quiet (`-q`, output-suppressed) shell probes \u2014 no files were modified.\n\n**What's in the workspace**\n\n| File | Size | Content | Line endings |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `state.txt` | 6 B | single line `draft` | LF |\n| `legacy.txt` | 28 B | `kind=example`, `status=draft` | **CRLF** |\n\n**Probe results**\n\n| Claim | Probe | Exit/Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `draft` present in `state.txt` | `grep -qx 'draft' state.txt` | **0 \u2014 confirmed** |\n| `kind=example` header present in `legacy.txt` | `grep -qx 'kind=example' legacy.txt` | **1 \u2014 false negative** |\n| same, with `\\r` stripped | `tr -d '\\r' < legacy.txt \\| grep -qx 'kind=example'` | **0 \u2014 confirmed** |\n| `status=draft` in `legacy.txt` (CR-stripped) | `tr -d '\\r' < legacy.txt \\| grep -qx 'status=draft'` | **0 \u2014 confirmed** |\n| combined assertion | all three above chained with `&&` | **ALL_OK \u2014 pass** |\n\n**Notes worth flagging**\n\n- The example header *is* present, but `legacy.txt` is CRLF-terminated (`od -c` shows `... e x a m p l e \\r \\n s t a t u s = d r a f t \\r \\n`). A naive exact-match probe fails against it; anchors like `$` and `-x` won't match until `\\r` is stripped. Any downstream parser for this file should be CR-tolerant.\n- Empty/unused tools: `awk` and `file` are unavailable in this environment (`awk: not found`; `/etc/magic` warnings), so verification relied on `grep`/`tr`/`od`.\n- Nothing to change \u2014 both the draft marker and the example header are confirmed present, so I made no edits."
